00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:27.420
Come in.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:28.700
Charlie Abel, over.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:36.720
What's the matter with your voice?

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:40.190
I'm eating a Mars bar.

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:44.800
Listen, we have found the black box.

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:47.820
It is locked, and we cannot find the key.

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:48.260
Over.

00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:51.030
Fennin might have it on him.

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:54.780
Still, I'd better not go down and ask him, had I?

00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:58.120
I'll tell you what.

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:00.000
Use the Oxy Assembly.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.960
Settle it. Over and out.

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:06.470
He's... Tucker, get the gear.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:10.060
Ken, get that mask. This thing can do your eyes up.

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:11.250
Go on.

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:18.350
Ken, me, me.

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:20.490
Sorry, Wolfie.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:27.480
OK, light it.

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:29.700
I ain't got lights, my fave.

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:33.050
No, nor have I. I thought you'd have brought a match with you.

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:35.050
Pucked up smoking, haven't I?

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:38.820
Hold on. I'll have a go with the gas fire.

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:43.590
It might be automatic.

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:45.450
On the other hand, it might not.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:54.990
Oh, I'm sick and tired of clips that don't bend and obviously acetylene gear that doesn't light.

00:20:54.990 --> 00:20:58.960
Ken, get the jellic diet.

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:04.900
It's a beautiful bridal gown, isn't it, Harold?

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:07.600
Oh, it's delightful, Florence.

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:09.660
Hey, that's Charles, is it?

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:10.600
Oh, no.

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:12.710
Charles isn't there.

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:15.130
This is my mum and dad's wedding.

00:21:16.570 --> 00:21:20.330
You saw our wedding in volume number six.

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:22.390
Five, Florence.

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:24.430
Volume number five.

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:27.750
Harold, did you know that we've got a dog?

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:29.540
No, Charles.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.480
He's a thoroughbred.

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:34.710
Really? We call him Fang.

00:21:34.710 --> 00:21:36.370
Well, there's a thing.

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:40.280
Oh, blimey, look at the time. I really must be going...

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:42.520
Oh, not this early.

00:21:52.280 --> 00:21:55.590
Er, what are you doing?

00:21:55.590 --> 00:22:00.000
What are you doing? I've told you, it's gonna be a little bang, all right?

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:01.620
Would you stop panicking?

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:05.580
Oh, hello?

00:22:06.030 --> 00:22:06.400
Hello?

00:22:07.170 --> 00:22:07.950
This is Red Leader.

00:22:08.150 --> 00:22:09.190
Come in, Charlie Abel.

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:09.710
Over.

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:11.520
Come in, Red Leader.

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:16.400
Listen, I'll fix the gelignite into the keyhole as instructed.

00:22:16.680 --> 00:22:16.920
Over.

00:22:17.670 --> 00:22:19.570
Did you use the right amount?

00:22:19.930 --> 00:22:20.210
Over.

00:22:20.830 --> 00:22:24.440
Yeah, a little blob the size of a thumbnail, like you said.

00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:24.900
Over.

00:22:25.270 --> 00:22:25.680
Good.

00:22:25.840 --> 00:22:29.290
Now, when it explodes, it'll make a loud popping sound.

00:22:29.510 --> 00:22:30.000
Don't believe...

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:37.520
alarmed. Anybody passing by or think it's a car backfiring? Over now. See what I mean,

00:22:37.640 --> 00:22:50.020
don't? When shall I fire it? Whenever you feel like it. Right, here goes then. Ten, nine,

00:22:50.020 --> 00:22:59.730
eight, seven, six, five, four, three, two, one.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.860
One. Zero.

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:11.680
Who's that?

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:20.030
Like a sunset, innit?

00:23:21.330 --> 00:23:22.410
Oh, it is.

00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:24.220
It's near the Railway Depot, innit?

00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:25.820
No, I'll speak further back than that.

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:28.050
Oh, what could it be, then?

00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:29.340
It's my pub.

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:30.000
Wow.

00:23:31.210 --> 00:23:32.730
Blimey, it is my pub.

00:23:33.650 --> 00:23:35.510
All right, Cyril, the pub's blown up.

00:23:35.630 --> 00:23:36.730
Quick, get...

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:37.210
How much?

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:55.090
Oh, my God.

00:23:56.600 --> 00:24:00.000
Smithy, don't think it was a car back file.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:09.530
Shut up, sucker.

00:24:09.530 --> 00:24:13.120
Oh, dear God.

00:24:13.120 --> 00:24:17.040
Oh, God.

00:24:17.040 --> 00:24:20.680
Oh, God.

00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:48.260
Don't be stupid, Tucker.

00:24:49.400 --> 00:24:52.740
Planning to be more suspicious if we didn't turn up, right?

00:24:52.960 --> 00:24:53.660
He's right, son.

00:24:54.380 --> 00:24:56.230
We don't just use this pub regular.

00:24:56.390 --> 00:24:57.780
For us, it's more like clocking on.

00:24:58.140 --> 00:24:58.340
Yeah.

00:24:58.600 --> 00:24:59.220
Usual, lads.

00:24:59.480 --> 00:25:00.000
Yeah, cheers, Ray.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:00.830
Tucka?

00:25:00.830 --> 00:25:01.720
Hey?

00:25:01.720 --> 00:25:02.920
King?

00:25:02.920 --> 00:25:06.470
Hey?

00:25:06.470 --> 00:25:10.370
Listen, if Fanny would have thought you had anything to do with this last night,

00:25:10.370 --> 00:25:13.400
he'd have been round to your house with a chainsaw.

00:25:13.400 --> 00:25:23.690
At least we've made something work.

00:25:23.690 --> 00:25:25.690
Here, I can buy shares in Fiat.

00:25:25.690 --> 00:25:28.710
There you go.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:33.200
I wonder what happened to Tophkin last night.

00:25:33.380 --> 00:25:35.420
As soon as he heard that bang, he had it away.

00:25:36.330 --> 00:25:38.510
He disappeared like a Prime Minister's promise.

00:25:39.780 --> 00:25:40.630
Eyes down, boys.

00:25:41.270 --> 00:25:43.690
Right, sweep that bookcase up.

00:25:44.770 --> 00:25:49.100
And Cyril, look around for a piece of paper with Trotsky's slate written on it, eh?

00:25:49.440 --> 00:25:50.460
It appears to be missing.

00:25:54.180 --> 00:25:55.260
Nasty business, eh?

00:25:55.540 --> 00:25:55.780
Yeah.

00:25:56.540 --> 00:25:57.760
Oh, it'll be nice when it's finished, though, Harry.

00:25:58.340 --> 00:25:58.660
Eh?

00:25:59.380 --> 00:25:59.800
Eh?

00:26:01.020 --> 00:26:03.490
talking about? My pub was blown up last night.

00:26:03.490 --> 00:26:08.150
You're joking. No. The entire back half was obliterated. What?

00:26:08.150 --> 00:26:11.870
Where were you then? I mean, they heard a bang in Watford. Oh, we were in, um...

00:26:11.870 --> 00:26:15.870
Birmingham. Birmingham. At a peace rally. That's right. It was great, Harry.

00:26:15.870 --> 00:26:19.630
We were sitting around this bonfire of harmony, eating soul food and eating,

00:26:19.630 --> 00:26:25.590
singing folk songs. It was great, wasn't it? Yeah. Sounds wonderful. What happened to your faces?

00:26:25.590 --> 00:26:29.320
I was a punch-up at the peace rally. It was shocking.

00:26:30.410 --> 00:26:33.740
You're all buried. Seems a bit scorched to me, Trotsky.

00:26:33.740 --> 00:26:37.160
Oh, I know, yeah. Someone threw it in the Bonfire of Harmony during the punch-up.

00:26:37.160 --> 00:26:41.110
What caused the explosion, Mr. Fennin? Any idea?

00:26:41.110 --> 00:26:44.300
Yeah, some burke left the gas fire on in my office.

00:26:44.300 --> 00:26:48.500
Shilts! I'm well covered. I should make a bob or two out of this.

00:26:48.500 --> 00:26:50.880
Insurance gain, tax loss, know what I mean?

00:26:50.880 --> 00:26:51.500
Yeah.

00:26:51.500 --> 00:26:53.620
Listen, have you seen anything of my cousin?

00:26:53.620 --> 00:26:55.320
Who? Charlie April?

00:26:55.320 --> 00:26:57.570
Who? Toph?

00:26:57.570 --> 00:27:00.000
Oh, Toph? No, no, and I've not seen him.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.520
since that night he was in here, Harry? No. Why, you ask?

00:27:02.520 --> 00:27:05.660
Well, I wouldn't be surprised if he didn't have something to do with this. I mean, he's

00:27:05.660 --> 00:27:10.260
hell-bent on revenge, isn't he? I mean, he's bent all round. They should never have let

00:27:10.260 --> 00:27:16.080
him out. Out of where, Harry? The Nathouse, of course.

00:27:16.080 --> 00:27:20.440
What? The Nathouse. I mean, after he tried to commit suicide, they chucked him out of

00:27:20.440 --> 00:27:30.000
the police force and into a loony bin. Proper policeman? Nah. Basically!

00:27:30.060 --> 00:27:32.060
He said he was an inspector in the blinds.

00:27:32.060 --> 00:27:34.060
That's why he said he had access to all the police departments.

00:27:34.060 --> 00:27:35.060
He did, yeah.

00:27:35.060 --> 00:27:37.060
His mind's gone, isn't it, eh?

00:27:37.060 --> 00:27:41.060
I mean, he spends most of his time wandering around the streets trying to arrest people.

00:27:41.060 --> 00:27:43.140
Mainly me.

00:27:43.140 --> 00:27:45.130
He had you one, Trotsky.

00:27:45.130 --> 00:27:46.020
Dear me.

00:27:46.020 --> 00:27:47.320
What a wally!

00:27:47.320 --> 00:27:51.340
What a wally!

00:27:51.340 --> 00:27:53.640
Oh, well.

00:27:53.640 --> 00:27:54.640
That's it then, lads, isn't it?

00:27:54.640 --> 00:27:56.940
I've been strung along by a madman.

00:27:56.940 --> 00:27:59.810
Well, me and Tucker are quite used to that.

00:27:59.810 --> 00:28:00.000
All right.

00:28:01.880 --> 00:28:06.090
Yes, Miffy. Just think of the damage we could have done if we hadn't have found out.

00:28:07.940 --> 00:28:11.650
Yeah, I think we've been very lucky, Tucker, yeah.

00:28:12.660 --> 00:28:15.200
Well, one thing for certain. Raise your glasses, boys.

00:28:15.740 --> 00:28:18.140
We've seen the last of that madman. What's his name? Tophkin.

00:28:18.640 --> 00:28:20.560
Oi, what's all this? Come on.

00:28:22.170 --> 00:28:23.150
Plan B.

00:28:25.850 --> 00:28:27.130
Great leader.
